  "content": {
    "title": "OU women's basketball season ends as South Carolina rolls in March Madness Sweet 16 rout",
    "text": "Updated March 28, 2026, 9:31 p.m. CTThe No. 4 seed Oklahoma Sooners will face the No. 1 seed South Carolina Gamecocks in the Sweet 16.This game is a rematch from January 22, when Oklahoma defeated South Carolina in overtime.The matchup features two of the nation's top offenses, with South Carolina ranked third and Oklahoma ranked fourth in scoring.The game is scheduled for Saturday at 4 p.m. CT at the Golden 1 Center in Sacramento.SACRAMENTO, CA — Jennie Baranczyk, crouched down in her signature spot on the court in front of the scorer’s table with her elbows resting on her knees, scratched her head.Oklahoma’s coach looked on with disapproval for most of the 40 minutes of gameplay inside Golden 1 Center, driving her heel into the hardwood or looking up to the rafters searching for answers after most plays.It was that kind of afternoon for the Sooners.No. 1 seed South Carolina was in control from the start of a dominating 94-68 win over No. 4 seed OU in the Sweet 16. Coach Dawn Staley and the Gamecocks have been inevitable for over half a decade, advancing to their sixth straight Elite Eight.On Saturday, it was the Ta’Niya Latson Show. The senior guard and Florida State transfer who is in her first season with South Carolina was an automatic bucket, finishing with 28 points on 4 for 4 shooting from 3-point range, while also knocking down 10 of 10 free throw attempts.As a team, the Gamecocks shot 10 for 14 from deep.The Sooners failed to match, finishing 6 for 20 from 3. Talented freshman guard Aaliyah Chavez scored 21 points and shot 8 for 21 from the field. Veterans Raegan Beers and Payton Verhulst — in their final games at OU — finished with 14 and 12, respectively.Perhaps the most bewildering thing? These Sooners beat South Carolina in overtime by 12 points just over two months ago.The Gamecocks clearly didn’t play their best then. Now? They have a chance to win the whole thing.For the second consecutive year, OU’s season ended in the Sweet 16 to a blue blood that overpowered them in every facet.Watch OU women's basketball live with FuboOklahoma vs South Carolina live score updatesEnd 3Q: South Carolina 68, Oklahoma 49 | Sooners trail by 19The Gamecocks lead the Sooners 68-49 at the end of the third quarter.South Carolina is 8 for 12 from 3.Aaliyah Chavez is up to 14 points for OU, while Raegan Beers and Payton Verhulst have 10 apiece.The Gamecocks are 10 minutes from the Elite Eight.HALF: South Carolina 47, Oklahoma 28 | Ta'Niya Latson, Raven Johnson combine for 34 pointsSouth Carolina dominated the first half.The Gamecocks lead 47-28 at halftime. South Carolina guards Raven Johnson and Ta'Niya Latson combined for 34 points in the first half.Oklahoma, which ranks first nationally in pace by CBB Analytics, was slowed down by the Gamecocks in the half. The Sooners failed to find any flow offensively and shot 33% compared to South Carolina's 52%.Aaliyah Chavez led OU with seven points on 3 for 12 shooting. She was also 1 for 5 from 3.Star center Raegan Beers had a quiet six points and three rebounds in the first half.End 1Q: South Carolina 23, Oklahoma 13 | Rough shooting start for SoonersOU is shooting just 32% through one quarter as it has struggled to find any flow offensively.Sooners freshman guard Aaliyah Chavez has seven but star center Raegan Beers finished the opening period with only two points on one shot attempt.The Gamecocks, meanwhile, started hot from 3. South Carolina is shooting 80% from deep. Probable starters for Oklahoma vs South Carolina in Women's NCAA Tournament Sweet 16OklahomaAaliyah Chavez, G, Fr.Zya Vann, G, So.Sahara Williams, F, Jr.Payton Verhulst, G, R-Sr.Raegan Beers, C, Sr.South CarolinaTa'Niya Latson, G, Sr.Tessa Johnson, G Jr.Joyce Edwards, F, So.Madina Okot, C, Sr.Raven Johnson, G, Sr.When does Oklahoma play in March Madness? What time is Sooners basketball game vs South Carolina in NCAA women's basketball tournament?Date: Saturday, March 28Time: 4 p.m. CTLocation: Golden 1 Center in Sacramento, CaliforniaWhat channel is Oklahoma vs South Carolina on today? How to watch, stream OU women's basketballTV: ESPNHow to watch online: Fubo (free trial)Oklahoma vs. South Carolina in NCAA Tournament score predictionSouth Carolina 93, Oklahoma 81: The Sooners keep it competitive early behind Aaliyah Chavez. But the Gamecocks' size and depth prove too much in the fourth quarter. Dawn Staley hasn’t lost in the Sweet 16 since 2019 and that won’t change Saturday.Oklahoma women's basketball schedule 2025-26All times are Central Standard Time (CST)Monday, Nov. 3: OU 84, Belmont 67Monday, Nov. 10: UCLA 73, OU 59Wednesday, Nov. 12: OU 89, Kansas City 61Friday, Nov. 14: OU 89, North Alabama 61Sunday, Nov. 16: OU 95, Western Carolina 32Wednesday, Nov. 19: OU 112, East Texas A&M 59Friday, Nov. 28: OU 100, Coppin State 46Sunday, Nov. 30: OU 109, Florida State 91Wednesday, Dec. 3: OU 103, NC State 98Sunday, Dec. 7: OU 90, Maryland Eastern Shore 37Thursday, Dec. 11: OU 103, Little Rock 48Saturday, Dec. 13: OU 92, OSU 70Monday, Dec. 22: OU 126, NC Central 54Thursday, Jan 1: OU 72, Texas A&M 50Sunday, Jan 4: OU 95, Mississippi State 47Thursday, Jan 8: Ole Miss 74, OU 69Sunday, Jan 11: Kentucky 63, OU 57Sunday, Jan 18: LSU 91, OU 72Thursday, Jan 22: OU 94, South Carolina 82 (OT)Sunday, Jan 25: OU 72, Auburn 65Thursday, Jan 29: OU 85, Texas A&M 58Sunday, Feb 1: Texas 78, OU 70Monday, Feb 9: Vanderbilt 102, OU 86Thursday, Feb 12: OU 81, Florida 74Sunday, Feb 15: OU 79, Alabama 71Thursday, Feb 19: OU 71, Georgia 67Sunday, Feb 22: OU 100, Tennessee 93Thursday, Feb 26: OU 89, Arkansas 44Sunday, Mar 1: OU 84, Missouri 78Thursday, Mar 5: SEC Tournament: OU 82, Florida 64Friday, Mar 6: SEC Tournament: LSU 112, OU 78Friday, Mar 20: Women's NCAA Tournament: OU 89, Idaho 59Sunday, March 22: Women's NCAA Tournament: OU 77, Michigan State 71Oklahoma vs South Carolina women's basketball highlightsIf X/Twitter feed doesn't load, click HERE.Colton Sulley covers the Oklahoma Sooners for The Oklahoman. Have a story idea for Colton? He can be reached at csulley@oklahoman.com or on X/Twitter at @colton_sulley. Support Colton's work and that of other Oklahoman journalists by purchasing a digital subscription today at subscribe.oklahoman.com.",
